# Shell scripts must stay LF, whatever platform the checkout happens on.
#
# core.autocrlf is true (it comes from the system gitconfig, not this repo)
# and there was no .gitattributes, so a fresh clone on Windows checked the
# four tracked .sh files out as 100% CRLF. Confirmed with a --no-checkout
# control clone of the parent commit.
#
# What CRLF does to these four, measured under GNU bash 5.2 on Linux:
#
#   set -euo pipefail  -> "set: pipefail^M: invalid option name", exit 2,
#                         aborts immediately. Only install-inbox-cron.sh.
#   set -uo pipefail   -> same error, then CARRIES ON and exits 0, with
#                         every variable CR-suffixed. verify-live.sh,
#                         setup-whatsapp.sh.
#   set -u             -> same, exits 0. resend_check.sh.
#
# So three of the four do NOT fail loudly. They run to completion, exit 0,
# and carry a trailing CR in every string - a URL, an ssh argument, a lock
# path. A redirect target gets it too: `cat > out.conf` writes `out.conf^M`,
# a different file, and the script reports success. verify-live.sh is the
# 374-check suite run after every deploy, so that is the worst place for it.
#
# None of this reproduces on Windows: Git for Windows patches its bash to
# strip the CR, so all four run fine in Git Bash. It only breaks on the VPS.
#
# Scoped to *.sh deliberately. A broad `* text=auto` would renormalize
# tracked files across the whole repo, and the HTML has mixed, per-file
# endings that nothing should rewrite in bulk.
#
# .php and .py are excluded on purpose: none carries a shebang or the exec
# bit, so they are only ever run as `php <file>` / `python <file>`, where the
# interpreter tolerates CRLF. Eleven .php files are already CRLF in the
# working tree and work fine.
*.sh text eol=lf

# dist/assets/ is the BUILT, SERVED artifact and its exact bytes are the
# thing being verified. The reasoning above that lets .php and .py tolerate
# CRLF does not transfer here: nothing interprets these files, they are
# served verbatim under a content-hashed name with max-age=31536000.
#
# tools/verify-live.sh:546 md5s the repo's copy of the homepage bundle
# against the bytes the site serves. Measured 23 Nov 2026: a fresh clone
# with core.autocrlf=true put 17 CRs into dist/assets/index-C6-wz3bb.js -
# 624142 -> 624159 bytes, md5 b4ef863c -> 79647fa7 - and the suite went red
# with "the live bundle differs from this checkout". That is a FALSE red
# caused by the checkout: the main checkout, the container and the live
# bytes through Cloudflare all agree on b4ef863c. A check that fails from a
# clean clone teaches people to ignore it.
#
# Deployment itself is unaffected - it is `git pull --ff-only` on the Linux
# VPS, which never applied the conversion. This is about any Windows
# checkout being a faithful copy of what is served, which is also what
# CLAUDE.md's post-build patching of this bundle (exact string swaps, and
# line-number-sensitive selectors in index.html) depends on.
#
# -text rather than binary: no conversion in either direction, still diffable.
dist/assets/** -text
